The #320 fix (moving the generated Rust code off `serde_yaml` onto `serde-saphyr`) passed the full gates when built on its own. I've put it back in the merge queue unchanged, as Jody asked on 2026-11-19.

- **The build passed but took 2h27m.** It ran as pipeline 3092027058 on commit 37df0c3, against main 509063b7. The full gates are budgeted at 100 minutes, and a batch without this change finished in 63. That probably explains the earlier "hangs": the batch builds that included #320 ran past the merge manager's 3-hour limit. They didn't actually hang.
- **I don't know why it's slow.** I can't read the build logs from here. I fuzzed `serde-saphyr` locally and every parse was fast (2 ms at worst), and the code under test barely reads YAML at runtime. One loose end: the dependency pin `2.1.1` lets cargo pick newer versions, so builds since 2026-11-18 have been using `serde-saphyr` 2.2.0, which switched to a different parser. That version hasn't been through a full gate run under its own build.
- **What's queued:** two commits, 1cbfe474 (the crate swap) and 37df0c39 (`STATE.md` only), on top of main 509063b7. I made no code changes in this run.

Next run, once the merge manager has posted its result on the issue:
- **If it merged:** post the outcome comment and close #320. There's no 2.6.x patch or backport, because the YAML the generated models write changed, so this ships in 2.7 as Jody ruled. The comment needs to say that, because the security exception llmproxy granted for this crate (llmproxy#56, expiring 2027-02-10) expects a 2.6.x release.
- **If a batch runs past 3 hours again:** tell Jody it passes on its own in 2h27m and ask whether it should be merged in a batch by itself.
